# Seeds for failure cases proptest has generated in the past. It is
# automatically read and these particular cases re-run before any
# novel cases are generated.
#
# It is recommended to check this file in to source control so that
# everyone who runs the test benefits from these saved cases.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What a `cc` line is, and what it is not
#
# It is a seed for the generator, not a recording of a schedule. Two
# consequences, both of which have been misread here:
#
# 1. A seed reproduces the ORIGINAL failing case; the comment records what that
#    case SHRANK to. They are different lengths and always were. A line whose
#    comment names five events regenerates the twenty-event schedule the search
#    first tripped on, which then shrinks again only if it still fails.
#
# 2. A seed decodes through the generator AS IT IS NOW. Adding an arm to
#    `arb_event` re-maps the whole random stream, so every line recorded before
#    that change regenerates something else entirely. Those are marked `found:`
#    below. They still run, and a random case is not worthless, but they no
#    longer reach the shape their comment describes and must not be read as
#    pins.
#
# The rule that follows: BEFORE adding an arm to `arb_event`, convert anything
# here that is load-bearing into a fixed-case test. Nothing is load-bearing
# today — every defect below has its own named pin, listed beside it — which is
# why this file could be relabelled rather than rewritten.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

